cases/td6_c1_c2_c3_high_q_total_f_k_repair_v89h4_aws_20260826/V87_HOSTILE_REVIEW.md:301:On `D(U H B3)`, `s` is a unit. Identity (1) writes `s` as a combination of the raw P12/FIRST rows plus `F h_F+sum_{e in E} q_e h_e`, and every coefficient of `h_F` and of each `h_e` lies in the registered localization (denominator `U H`). If a DVR arc in this retained family kills every raw row and puts `F` and all 22 licensed q coordinates in the maximal ideal, the right side has positive valuation and the left side does not.
