+## Executive judgment
+
+The new results are real structural progress, but sharpen rather than remove the campaign's oldest danger. Three local mechanisms now look reusable: D1 turns a source-support ceiling into a uniform contradiction by an odd-pole functional; affine-Faber recursion reduces repeatedly to a small predecessor state followed by an intrinsic cubic; TD6 FIRST matrices admit polynomial normalization, leaving P12 as the nonlinear compatibility datum.
+
+The earliest possible fatal gap remains **landing/fidelity**. No promoted theorem sends every hypothetical Keller counterexample, including closed degenerations and omitted source moduli, into the union of the local charts being emptied. This gap occurs before the remaining finite D1 cells, affine-Faber equality faces, and TD6 total-`F` interpretation. A complete local exclusion inside a non-cofinal atlas does not advance JC2. The next day should spend at least as much top-quality attention on a proof-carrying total-Rees atlas and its valuative completeness as on further local eliminations.
+
+My strongest new synthesis is that the three branches may be instances of one filtered presentation: the degree-zero differential is unimodular, higher filtration support is controlled by a finite directed graph, and the final obstruction is a scalar cokernel class. D1's odd functional is a dual cokernel class; affine-Faber predecessors are transitions between associated-graded presentations; TD6's determinant-one FIRST block is a chain contraction candidate. This is exact as an organizational reformulation once the matrices are written; the claimed common theorem is conjectural.
